WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.064 --> 00:00:02.610
- [Narrator] This is the F-16 fighter jet,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:06.030
developed by the US with a
number of European partners.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.330
And this is the Su-35, the
Russian equivalent being deployed

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.040
in the Ukraine War.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.440
Kyiv says it wants 200 western jets,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.310
such as the Eurofighter Typhoon,
F-16, or Swedish Gripen,

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.170
so they can dominate the skies.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:24.170
- We have freedom, give
us wings to protect it.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.590
- [Narrator] And while the US has said

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.450
it won't give fighter jets to Kyiv,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.390
the UK and some European
countries are now considering

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.550
sending combat aircraft.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.410
- Any decision to send or
to supply combat aircraft

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.870
would inevitably be significant.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.550
- [Narrator] So what
capabilities could western jets

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.450
give Ukraine?

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.150
And how do they compare to
the main Russian jet deployed

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:45.983
in the war?

00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:48.180
(jet engine roaring)

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.180
First, let's look at why western
jets are important to Kyiv.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.480
So far, neither Ukraine nor Russia

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.430
has achieved air superiority.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.220
That's an air force's ability
to take control of the sky,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.140
stopping anybody other than themselves

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.240
from entering a particular airspace.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.350
At the start of the war,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.410
Moscow had nearly 1,200
combat-capable aircraft,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.750
according to the IISS Think Tank.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.640
That was far more than Kyiv's inventory

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.820
of around 120 aging Soviet-era aircraft.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.360
- So the challenge for Ukraine
is its combat air inventory

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.730
is increasingly difficult to maintain.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.250
In a combat environment, you really need

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.880
as many of your aircraft
available and on the flight line

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.553
as you can have, almost round the clock.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.730
- [Narrator] To avoid
using their limited jets,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.950
Ukraine has focused on its air defenses,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.560
shooting down over a hundred
Russian planes and helicopters

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.450
with surface-to-air missiles.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.820
This has made Moscow
reluctant to send its own jets

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.320
beyond the frontline.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.200
Analysts say it's mainly used
the long-range capabilities

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.320
of its air force to strike
Ukrainian targets from afar.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.290
- So one of the challenges
the Ukrainians have is

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.960
that their Soviet-era air-to-air missiles,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.440
particularly the
beyond-visual-range weapons

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.740
don't have anything like
the engagement range

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.980
that the Russian combat
aircraft do at the moment.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.020
- [Narrator] Experts say
western jets would allow Kyiv

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.180
to counter Russia's air force directly,

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.330
changing the balance
of power in the skies.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.620
So, let's look at the specifics

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.990
of how these jets operate
on the battlefield.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.780
Russia's Su-35 is larger
than the aircraft Ukraine

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.310
could receive from its allies,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.860
allowing it to carry a
bigger weapon's payload.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.750
It's also equipped with a passive sensor

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.960
that can spot opposing jets
without being detected itself.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.510
Paired with long-range missiles
that can fire at targets

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.950
over 60 miles away,

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.070
analysts say it's had a
distinct advantage in medium

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.350
and long-range aerial encounters

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.800
against Ukraine's current
inventory of Soviet-era aircraft.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.650
But western jets, such as
the F-16, would come equipped

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.780
with advanced medium-range missiles,

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.330
including the American AIM-120.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.030
Analysts say these weapons
could level the playing field,

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.160
allowing Ukraine to more
effectively challenge

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.073
Russia's air force in medium
and long-range encounters.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.160
But when it comes to air power,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.110
it's not just the systems that matter.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.780
The person piloting the
jet is just as important.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.390
Experts say Ukraine's pilots
will need extensive training

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.080
for up to a year to use any
western aircraft effectively.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.000
- You can't just take somebody out

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.450
of a Soviet-design combat
aircraft and expect them

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.060
to be able to fight to the
same level the next day.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.670
Even for an experienced fast-jet pilot,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.430
there is a period of
conversion and just to get used

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.680
to the aircraft, its
displays, how it handles,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.620
and then you also gotta learn
how to fight the aircraft.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.700
- [Narrator] So the UK has agreed

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.710
to start training Ukrainian pilots,

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.220
as Kyiv continues to press its
allies into providing jets.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.650
Western governments are nervous
that providing the weapons,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.020
which could be used to
hit targets inside Russia,

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.948
could escalate the war.

00:03:41.948 --> 00:03:42.930
(missile firing)

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.760
But analysts say that any model of jet

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.890
would complement the arsenal of weaponry,

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.480
including HIMARS and tanks,

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.047
that Kyiv is already
receiving from its allies.

00:03:51.047 --> 00:03:53.547
(tense music)

